### 1. Get all students (PostgreSQL)
GET http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=postgres

### 2. Get all students (SQL Server)
GET http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=sqlserver


### 3. Create student - Success (PostgreSQL)
POST http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": 40110001,
  "firstName": "Mehdi",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 18.5
}

### 4. Create student - Success (SQL Server)
POST http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=sqlserver
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": 40110002,
  "firstName": "Sara",
  "isMale": false,
  "grade": 19.25
}

### 5. Create student - Fail (Duplicate Student Number -> Expects 409 Conflict)
POST http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": 40110001,
  "firstName": "Mehdi Duplicate",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 15.0
}

### 6. Create student - Fail (Invalid Student Number <= 0 -> Expects 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": -5,
  "firstName": "Ali",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 17.0
}

### 7. Create student - Fail (First Name > 50 characters -> Expects 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": 40110003,
  "firstName": "ThisIsAVeryLongNameThatExceedsTheFiftyCharacterLimitAllowedByTheDatabaseSchema",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 16.0
}

### 8. Create student - Fail (Grade > 20 -> Expects 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": 40110004,
  "firstName": "Reza",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 22.5
}

### 9. Create student - Fail (Grade < 0 -> Expects 400 Bad Request)
POST http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentNumber": 40110005,
  "firstName": "Mina",
  "isMale": false,
  "grade": -2.0
}


### 10. Get student by ID (PostgreSQL)
GET http://localhost:5052/api/students/40110001?db=postgres

### 11. Get student by ID (SQL Server)
GET http://localhost:5052/api/students/40110002?db=sqlserver


### 12. Update student - Success (PostgreSQL)
PUT http://localhost:5052/api/students/40110001?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ahmad",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 19.75
}

### 13. Update student - Fail (Invalid Route ID <= 0 -> Expects 400 Bad Request)
PUT http://localhost:5052/api/students/0?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ahmad",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 19.75
}

### 14. Update student - Fail (First Name > 50 characters -> Expects 400 Bad Request)
PUT http://localhost:5052/api/students/40110001?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "ThisIsAVeryLongNameThatExceedsTheFiftyCharacterLimitAllowedByTheDatabaseSchema",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 18.0
}

### 15. Update student - Fail (Grade > 20 -> Expects 400 Bad Request)
PUT http://localhost:5052/api/students/40110001?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ahmad",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 25.0
}

### 16. Update student - Fail (Student Not Found -> Expects 404 Not Found)
PUT http://localhost:5052/api/students/99999999?db=postgres
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Ghost",
  "isMale": true,
  "grade": 15.0
}


### 17. Delete student - Success (PostgreSQL)
DELETE http://localhost:5052/api/students/40110001?db=postgres

### 18. Delete student - Fail (Student Not Found -> Expects 404 Not Found)
DELETE http://localhost:5052/api/students/99999999?db=postgres


### 19. Invalid database parameter (Expects 400 Bad Request)
GET http://localhost:5052/api/students?db=oracle

